		summary = 'The **Outback** is a remote, vast, sparsely populated area of [[Australia]]. It is more remote than what Australians call “the bush”. While often envisaged as being [[Aridity|arid]], the Outback regions extend from the northern to southern Australian coastlines and encompass a number of climatic zones, including [[Tropical climate|tropical]] and monsoonal climates in northern areas, arid areas in the "red centre" and semi-arid and [[Temperate climate|temperate]] climates in southerly regions. The total population is estimated at 607,000 people.',
